cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use avgen in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "avgen: a PyTorch-native framework for training video and audio-video generation models at scale"
abstract: >-
  avgen is an open-source PyTorch framework for pretraining, finetuning,
  inference, and reinforcement-learning post-training of video and audio-video
  diffusion transformers. Its model interior is sequence-first: dense latent
  grids exist only at the data and codec boundary, and everything in between is
  a token stream carrying explicit physical coordinates, which is what makes
  context parallelism and variable-resolution batching possible. Distributed
  execution is entirely PyTorch-native, composing five explicit parallelism axes
  (replicated data, sharded data, context, tensor, and pipeline) over DeviceMesh
  and DTensor, with FSDP2, ring attention, and resharding Distributed
  Checkpoints. avgen also ships a simulator that validates a parallelism plan at
  any world size on a single CPU machine, so a thousand-GPU configuration can be
  reviewed before it is launched.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/avgen-project/avgen"
